{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Session 2 — Construction of the finite element method\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Triangular meshes, local shape functions, assembly, and numerical integration\"\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "toc: true\n",
        "number-sections: true\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning objectives {.unnumbered}\n",
        "\n",
        "By the end of this session, students should be able to:\n",
        "\n",
        "- define a \\(P_1\\) finite-element approximation space on a triangular mesh;\n",
        "- construct linear nodal shape functions directly on a physical triangle;\n",
        "- derive the elemental stiffness matrix and elemental load vector;\n",
        "- explain how local element contributions are assembled into a global linear system;\n",
        "- relate local support of the basis functions to matrix sparsity;\n",
        "- impose homogeneous and non-homogeneous Dirichlet boundary conditions;\n",
        "- understand the practical role of the reference element, affine mapping, gradient transformation, and numerical quadrature.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Schedule {.unnumbered}\n",
        "\n",
        "| Time | Topic |\n",
        "|---:|---|\n",
        "| 0–15 min | Triangular mesh and definition of \\(V_h\\) |\n",
        "| 15–35 min | \\(P_1\\) shape functions on one physical triangle |\n",
        "| 35–50 min | Elemental stiffness matrix and load vector |\n",
        "| 50–60 min | Global basis functions and assembly |\n",
        "| 60–70 min | Local support, sparsity, and Dirichlet conditions |\n",
        "| 70–90 min | Technical block: reference element, mapping, and quadrature |\n",
        "\n",
        "# Triangular mesh and finite-element space\n",
        "\n",
        "Let\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\Omega \\subset \\mathbb{R}^2\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "be approximated by a triangulation\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathcal{T}_h\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\{T_1,T_2,\\ldots,T_{N_e}\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The domain is decomposed into non-overlapping triangles:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\Omega_h\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\bigcup_{T\\in\\mathcal{T}_h} T.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For linear triangular finite elements, we define\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "V_h\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\left\\{\n",
        "v_h\\in C^0(\\Omega_h):\n",
        "v_h|_T\\in\\mathbb{P}_1(T)\n",
        "\\quad\n",
        "\\forall T\\in\\mathcal{T}_h\n",
        "\\right\\}.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus, a finite-element function is:\n",
        "\n",
        "- continuous over the whole mesh;\n",
        "- affine on each individual triangle.\n",
        "\n",
        "The finite-element approximation is written\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "u_h(x,y)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^{N_h}\n",
        "U_i\\phi_i(x,y),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where the global nodal basis functions satisfy\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\phi_i(\\mathbf{x}_j)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\delta_{ij}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Hence,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "U_i=u_h(\\mathbf{x}_i).\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The coefficients of the finite-element approximation are therefore the nodal values of the approximate solution.\n",
        "\n",
        "# \\(P_1\\) shape functions on one physical triangle\n",
        "\n",
        "Consider one triangle\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "T\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\operatorname{conv}\n",
        "\\{\n",
        "\\mathbf{x}_1,\\mathbf{x}_2,\\mathbf{x}_3\n",
        "\\},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "with\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbf{x}_a=(x_a,y_a),\n",
        "\\qquad a=1,2,3.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Inside \\(T\\), the finite-element solution is affine. If the three local vertices correspond to global nodes \\(i_1,i_2,i_3\\),\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "u_h|_T(x,y)\n",
        "=\n",
        "U_{i_1}N_1(x,y)\n",
        "+\n",
        "U_{i_2}N_2(x,y)\n",
        "+\n",
        "U_{i_3}N_3(x,y).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The local shape functions are affine:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "N_a(x,y)\n",
        "=\n",
        "a_a+b_a x+c_a y,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "and satisfy the nodal interpolation conditions\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "N_a(\\mathbf{x}_b)=\\delta_{ab},\n",
        "\\qquad a,b=1,2,3.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For example,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "N_1(\\mathbf{x}_1)=1,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "N_1(\\mathbf{x}_2)=N_1(\\mathbf{x}_3)=0,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "and similarly for \\(N_2\\) and \\(N_3\\).\n",
        "\n",
        "## Explicit construction\n",
        "\n",
        "For each shape function\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "N_a(x,y)=a_a+b_a x+c_a y,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "the coefficients are obtained from\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "1 & x_1 & y_1\\\\\n",
        "1 & x_2 & y_2\\\\\n",
        "1 & x_3 & y_3\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "a_a\\\\\n",
        "b_a\\\\\n",
        "c_a\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\mathbf e_a,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where \\(\\mathbf e_a\\) is the \\(a\\)-th vector of the canonical basis of \\(\\mathbb R^3\\).\n",
        "\n",
        "Because the shape functions are affine,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\nabla N_a\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "b_a\\\\\n",
        "c_a\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "is constant over the triangle.\n",
        "\n",
        "This property makes the \\(P_1\\) Poisson element particularly simple.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Elemental stiffness matrix\n",
        "\n",
        "For the Poisson problem,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "-\\Delta u=f,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "the weak form contains the bilinear form\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "a(u,v)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_\\Omega\n",
        "\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v\\,d\\Omega.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "On one triangle \\(T\\), the elemental stiffness matrix is defined by\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{ab}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_T\n",
        "\\nabla N_a\\cdot\\nabla N_b\\,d\\Omega,\n",
        "\\qquad a,b=1,2,3.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Since the gradients of the \\(P_1\\) shape functions are constant on \\(T\\),\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{ab}\n",
        "=\n",
        "|T|\\,\n",
        "\\nabla N_a\\cdot\\nabla N_b.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The full elemental matrix is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K^{(T)}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{11} & K^{(T)}_{12} & K^{(T)}_{13}\\\\\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{21} & K^{(T)}_{22} & K^{(T)}_{23}\\\\\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{31} & K^{(T)}_{32} & K^{(T)}_{33}\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "# Elemental load vector\n",
        "\n",
        "The right-hand side of the weak formulation is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\ell(v)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_\\Omega f v\\,d\\Omega.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "On one triangle,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "F_a^{(T)}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_T fN_a\\,d\\Omega,\n",
        "\\qquad a=1,2,3.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F^{(T)}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "F_1^{(T)}\\\\\n",
        "F_2^{(T)}\\\\\n",
        "F_3^{(T)}\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For constant \\(f\\),\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\int_T N_a\\,d\\Omega\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{|T|}{3},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "and therefore\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "F^{(T)}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{f|T|}{3}\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "1\\\\\n",
        "1\\\\\n",
        "1\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For a general \\(f(x,y)\\), the integral is usually evaluated numerically.\n",
        "\n",
        "> **FEM localizes both approximation and integration.**\n",
        "\n",
        "# From local to global basis functions\n",
        "\n",
        "A global nodal basis function \\(\\phi_i\\) is obtained by joining the local shape functions associated with node \\(i\\) over all triangles containing that node.\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\phi_i(\\mathbf{x}_j)=\\delta_{ij},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "and\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{supp}\\phi_i\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\bigcup\n",
        "\\left\\{\n",
        "T\\in\\mathcal{T}_h:\n",
        "\\mathbf{x}_i\\in T\n",
        "\\right\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The support of \\(\\phi_i\\) is therefore local.\n",
        "\n",
        "The global approximation is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "u_h\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^{N_h}\n",
        "U_i\\phi_i.\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "11776d0f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-gmsh-mesh\n",
        "#| fig-cap: Coarse triangular mesh of a square domain containing a circular hole.\n",
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "\n",
        "import gmsh\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import matplotlib.tri as mtri\n",
        "\n",
        "gmsh.initialize()\n",
        "gmsh.model.add(\"square_with_hole\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Geometry\n",
        "L = 1.0\n",
        "R = 0.18\n",
        "\n",
        "square = gmsh.model.occ.addRectangle(0, 0, 0, L, L)\n",
        "hole = gmsh.model.occ.addDisk(0.5, 0.5, 0, R, R)\n",
        "gmsh.model.occ.cut([(2, square)], [(2, hole)])\n",
        "gmsh.model.occ.synchronize()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Deliberately coarse mesh for visualization\n",
        "gmsh.option.setNumber(\"Mesh.MeshSizeMin\", 0.16)\n",
        "gmsh.option.setNumber(\"Mesh.MeshSizeMax\", 0.22)\n",
        "gmsh.model.mesh.generate(2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Extract nodes\n",
        "node_tags, node_coords, _ = gmsh.model.mesh.getNodes()\n",
        "coords = node_coords.reshape(-1, 3)\n",
        "x = coords[:, 0]\n",
        "y = coords[:, 1]\n",
        "\n",
        "tag_to_index = {\n",
        "    tag: i for i, tag in enumerate(node_tags)\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "# Extract 3-node triangles\n",
        "element_types, _, element_nodes = gmsh.model.mesh.getElements(dim=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "triangles = None\n",
        "\n",
        "for element_type, nodes in zip(element_types, element_nodes):\n",
        "    if element_type == 2:  # Gmsh type 2 = 3-node linear triangle\n",
        "        nodes = nodes.reshape(-1, 3)\n",
        "        triangles = np.array([\n",
        "            [tag_to_index[tag] for tag in tri]\n",
        "            for tri in nodes\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "        break\n",
        "\n",
        "gmsh.finalize()\n",
        "\n",
        "mesh = mtri.Triangulation(x, y, triangles)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
        "plt.triplot(mesh, linewidth=0.8)\n",
        "plt.plot(x, y, \".\", markersize=3)\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"$x$\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"$y$\")\n",
        "plt.gca().set_aspect(\"equal\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-gmsh-mesh",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The following figure selects one triangle and displays the three **global**\n",
        "basis functions associated with its three vertices."
      ],
      "id": "c7ca3c9b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-three-global-basis\n",
        "#| fig-cap: Three global $P_1$ basis functions associated with the vertices of one triangle.\n",
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "\n",
        "# Select a triangle whose centroid is close to this point\n",
        "target_point = np.array([0.25, 0.50])\n",
        "\n",
        "centroids_x = x[triangles].mean(axis=1)\n",
        "centroids_y = y[triangles].mean(axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "triangle_id = np.argmin(\n",
        "    (centroids_x - target_point[0])**2\n",
        "    + (centroids_y - target_point[1])**2\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "selected_nodes = triangles[triangle_id]\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(15, 4.5))\n",
        "\n",
        "for a, node in enumerate(selected_nodes):\n",
        "    phi = np.zeros(len(x))\n",
        "    phi[node] = 1.0\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, a + 1, projection=\"3d\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax.plot_trisurf(\n",
        "        mesh,\n",
        "        phi,\n",
        "        edgecolor=\"black\",\n",
        "        linewidth=0.5,\n",
        "        alpha=0.9\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax.scatter([x[node]], [y[node]], [1.0], s=50)\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax.set_xlabel(\"$x$\")\n",
        "    ax.set_ylabel(\"$y$\")\n",
        "    ax.set_zlabel(r\"$\\phi_i$\")\n",
        "    ax.set_zlim(0, 1.05)\n",
        "    ax.set_title(rf\"Global basis function $\\phi_{{i_{a+1}}}$\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-three-global-basis",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Assembly of the global system\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose the local nodes\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "1,\\qquad 2,\\qquad 3\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "of one triangle correspond to the global nodes\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "5,\\qquad 12,\\qquad 8.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then the elemental stiffness matrix is assembled by adding its entries to the corresponding entries of the global matrix:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "K_{5,5} & K_{5,12} & K_{5,8}\\\\\n",
        "K_{12,5} & K_{12,12} & K_{12,8}\\\\\n",
        "K_{8,5} & K_{8,12} & K_{8,8}\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "\\; += \\;\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{11} & K^{(T)}_{12} & K^{(T)}_{13}\\\\\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{21} & K^{(T)}_{22} & K^{(T)}_{23}\\\\\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{31} & K^{(T)}_{32} & K^{(T)}_{33}\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Similarly,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "F_5\\\\\n",
        "F_{12}\\\\\n",
        "F_8\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "\\; += \\;\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "F^{(T)}_1\\\\\n",
        "F^{(T)}_2\\\\\n",
        "F^{(T)}_3\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "After assembling all triangles,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{KU=F.}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "# Local support and sparsity\n",
        "\n",
        "The global stiffness entries are\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K_{ij}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_\\Omega\n",
        "\\nabla\\phi_i\\cdot\\nabla\\phi_j\\,d\\Omega.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If two nodal basis functions do not overlap,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{supp}\\phi_i\n",
        "\\cap\n",
        "\\operatorname{supp}\\phi_j\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\varnothing,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K_{ij}=0.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{local support}\n",
        "\\Longrightarrow\n",
        "\\text{sparse global matrix}.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Only nodes that belong to at least one common element can interact directly through the stiffness matrix.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Dirichlet boundary conditions\n",
        "\n",
        "## Homogeneous Dirichlet conditions\n",
        "\n",
        "For\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "u=0\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\text{on }\\Gamma_D,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "the coefficients associated with Dirichlet nodes are prescribed:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "U_i=0\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\text{for all nodes }i\\text{ on }\\Gamma_D.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The remaining degrees of freedom are unknown.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Non-homogeneous Dirichlet conditions\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose instead that\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "u=g\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\text{on }\\Gamma_D.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Split the degrees of freedom into\n",
        "\n",
        "- \\(U_f\\): unknown (free) degrees of freedom;\n",
        "- \\(U_D\\): prescribed Dirichlet degrees of freedom.\n",
        "\n",
        "After grouping the corresponding rows and columns, write\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "K_{ff} & K_{fD}\\\\\n",
        "K_{Df} & K_{DD}\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "U_f\\\\\n",
        "U_D\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "F_f\\\\\n",
        "F_D\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The Dirichlet values are known:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "U_D=g_D.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Substituting them into the equations corresponding to the unknown degrees of freedom gives\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K_{ff}U_f+K_{fD}g_D=F_f,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "hence\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "K_{ff}U_f\n",
        "=\n",
        "F_f-K_{fD}g_D.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The term \\(-K_{fD}g_D\\) is the algebraic lifting of the non-homogeneous Dirichlet data.\n",
        "\n",
        "After solving for \\(U_f\\), the complete vector is reconstructed as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "U=\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "U_f\\\\\n",
        "g_D\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "# Technical block — reference element, mapping, and quadrature\n",
        "\n",
        "The previous derivation was carried out directly on a physical triangle. This is sufficient to understand the finite-element construction.\n",
        "\n",
        "In practical finite-element software, however, element integrals are evaluated systematically by mapping every physical triangle to the same reference triangle.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Reference triangle\n",
        "\n",
        "Define\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\widehat T\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\left\\{\n",
        "(\\xi,\\eta):\n",
        "\\xi\\ge0,\\;\n",
        "\\eta\\ge0,\\;\n",
        "\\xi+\\eta\\le1\n",
        "\\right\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Its vertices are\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(0,0),\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "(1,0),\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "(0,1).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The \\(P_1\\) shape functions on the reference triangle are\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\widehat N_1=1-\\xi-\\eta,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\widehat N_2=\\xi,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\widehat N_3=\\eta.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Affine mapping\n",
        "\n",
        "A physical triangle \\(T\\), with vertices\n",
        "\\(\\mathbf x_1,\\mathbf x_2,\\mathbf x_3\\), is obtained from \\(\\widehat T\\) through\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbf x(\\xi,\\eta)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\mathbf x_1\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\xi(\\mathbf x_2-\\mathbf x_1)\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\eta(\\mathbf x_3-\\mathbf x_1).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Its Jacobian is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "J\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(\\xi,\\eta)}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "x_2-x_1 & x_3-x_1\\\\\n",
        "y_2-y_1 & y_3-y_1\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The area element transforms as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "d\\Omega\n",
        "=\n",
        "|\\det J|\\,d\\xi\\,d\\eta.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\int_T g(x,y)\\,d\\Omega\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_{\\widehat T}\n",
        "g(\\mathbf x(\\xi,\\eta))\n",
        "|\\det J|\n",
        "\\,d\\xi\\,d\\eta.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Transformation of gradients\n",
        "\n",
        "If\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "N_a(x,y)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\widehat N_a(\\xi,\\eta),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "the chain rule gives\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\nabla_{\\xi}\\widehat N_a\n",
        "=\n",
        "J^T\\nabla_x N_a.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Hence,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\nabla_x N_a\n",
        "=\n",
        "J^{-T}\\nabla_{\\xi}\\widehat N_a.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For an affine \\(P_1\\) triangle, \\(J\\) is constant over the element.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Numerical quadrature on the reference triangle\n",
        "\n",
        "An integral over the reference triangle is approximated by a sum over quadrature points:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\int_{\\widehat T}\n",
        "g(\\xi,\\eta)\\,d\\xi\\,d\\eta\n",
        "\\approx\n",
        "\\sum_{q=1}^{n_q}\n",
        "w_q\\,g(\\xi_q,\\eta_q).\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Combining quadrature with the affine mapping gives\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\int_T g(x,y)\\,d\\Omega\n",
        "\\approx\n",
        "\\sum_{q=1}^{n_q}\n",
        "w_q\\,\n",
        "g(\\mathbf x_q)\\,\n",
        "|\\det J_q|,\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbf x_q\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\mathbf x(\\xi_q,\\eta_q).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For an affine triangle, \\(J_q=J\\) at every quadrature point.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Poisson stiffness matrix in practice\n",
        "\n",
        "For\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{ab}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\int_T\n",
        "\\nabla N_a\\cdot\\nabla N_b\\,d\\Omega,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "the practical quadrature formula is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "K^{(T)}_{ab}\n",
        "\\approx\n",
        "\\sum_{q=1}^{n_q}\n",
        "w_q\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "J_q^{-T}\\nabla_{\\xi}\\widehat N_a(\\xi_q,\\eta_q)\n",
        "\\right)\n",
        "\\cdot\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "J_q^{-T}\\nabla_{\\xi}\\widehat N_b(\\xi_q,\\eta_q)\n",
        "\\right)\n",
        "|\\det J_q|.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Similarly, the elemental load vector is computed as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "F_a^{(T)}\n",
        "\\approx\n",
        "\\sum_{q=1}^{n_q}\n",
        "w_q\\,\n",
        "f(\\mathbf x_q)\\,\n",
        "\\widehat N_a(\\xi_q,\\eta_q)\\,\n",
        "|\\det J_q|.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "For the simplest one-point quadrature rule on \\(\\widehat T\\),\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(\\xi_1,\\eta_1)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\left(\n",
        "\\frac13,\\frac13\n",
        "\\right),\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "w_1=\\frac12.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\int_{\\widehat T}\n",
        "g(\\xi,\\eta)\\,d\\xi\\,d\\eta\n",
        "\\approx\n",
        "\\frac12\n",
        "g\\left(\\frac13,\\frac13\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This rule is exact for affine functions. In particular, it is exact for the\n",
        "\\(P_1\\) stiffness integrand, which is constant on an affine triangle.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Practical finite-element algorithm\n",
        "\n",
        "For the Poisson problem, a basic finite-element code follows this sequence:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Generate a triangular mesh.\n",
        "2. Define the nodal degrees of freedom.\n",
        "3. For each triangle \\(T\\):\n",
        "   - identify its global node numbers;\n",
        "   - compute \\(K^{(T)}\\);\n",
        "   - compute \\(F^{(T)}\\);\n",
        "   - add these contributions to the global \\(K\\) and \\(F\\).\n",
        "4. Impose Dirichlet boundary conditions.\n",
        "5. Solve the reduced linear system.\n",
        "6. Reconstruct\n",
        "\n",
        "   $$\n",
        "   u_h(x,y)\n",
        "   =\n",
        "   \\sum_i U_i\\phi_i(x,y).\n",
        "   $$\n",
        "\n",
        "The central computational structure is therefore\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{mesh}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{local approximation}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{element integrals}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{assembly}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{sparse global system}.\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "# Further reading\n",
        "\n",
        "Useful topics for understanding practical finite-element implementations in more detail include:\n",
        "\n",
        "- barycentric coordinates;\n",
        "- mapping between reference and physical elements;\n",
        "- transformation of gradients;\n",
        "- Gaussian quadrature on triangles;\n",
        "- higher-order elements;\n",
        "- isoparametric elements."
      ],
      "id": "92453179"
    }
